    "html": "\n  <div class=\"hero-meta\"><span class=\"level-badge\" data-level=\"2\">Level 2 - Beginner</span><span class=\"time\">20 min</span><span class=\"chip warn\">Medium</span><span class=\"chip accent\">BST: in-order is sorted</span><a class=\"chip\" href=\"https://leetcode.com/problems/kth-smallest-element-in-a-bst/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">LC 230</a></div>\n  <h1>Kth Smallest Element in a BST</h1>\n  <p class=\"lead\">Insight in one line: an in-order walk of a binary search tree visits the values in sorted order, so the k-th node it visits is the answer. Do the walk with an explicit stack and stop the moment the counter hits k: O(h + k) time, O(h) space. If the tree changes and the query repeats, store subtree sizes in each node and answer in O(h).</p>\n"
